1. In google search "argocd install"

2. Select "https://argo-cd.readthedocs.io/en/stable/operator-manual/installation/"

3. kubectl create ns argocd

4. kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml

5. kubens argocd    # To switch the namespace from default to argocd

Note: I want to access argocd-server, by default it is in ClusterIP, I want to convert ClusterIP into Nodeport
We can do it using kubectl edit
But we need to change only 1 field i.e. ClusterIP, so we can use patch i.e. kubectl patch

6. kubectl patch svc argocd-server -n argocd -p '{"spec":{"type":"NodePort"}}'

7. <publicIP:portNum> {13.127.106.106:32467} to connect to argocd

8. To get the crendiatials to login into argocd, we use secrets

9. kubectl get secrets

10. To get password, use the following command: 
kubectl describe secrets argocd-initial-admin-secret

Output:
-------
Name:         argocd-initial-admin-secret
Namespace:    argocd
Labels:       <none>
Annotations:  <none>

Type:  Opaque

Data
====
password:  16 bytes

Note: If I use the above command, in the output we will not be able to see password as it is encoded

11. To get password which is in base64 format, use the following command: 
kubectl get secrets -n argocd argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath='{.data.password}'

Output:
-------
UXhMUWhxYXRObWxrRGVzaQ==

12. To convert the above output from base64 to normal(actual password), use the following command:
kubectl get secrets -n argocd argocd-initial-admin-secret -o jsonpath='{.data.password}' | base64 -d
